Activation steps for natedev:
- Pick a time with no CI run; the rebuild restarts both GitHub runners.
- Before the rebuild, prove the proposed runner sandbox can open steve:
  `sudo systemd-run --wait --collect --pipe -p User=hana-linux-1 -p PrivateDevices=yes -p DevicePolicy=closed -p 'DeviceAllow=char-rtc r' -p 'DeviceAllow=/dev/steve rw' -p BindPaths=-/dev/steve /bin/sh -c 'exec 3<>/dev/steve && echo OPEN_OK'`.
  It must print `OPEN_OK`.
- After the rebuild, `systemctl --user status sccache` must show active;
  `cat /proc/$(systemctl --user show --property=MainPID --value sccache)/cgroup`
  must end in `builds.slice/sccache.service` for the service's main process.
- Read `zramctl` and `oomctl`; check the next CI job log has no
  `failed to connect to jobserver` warning. Only then consider removing
  `CARGO_BUILD_JOBS` in a later change.

